# The hook scripts must keep LF endings in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says: a strict POSIX shell (dash, as on
# Linux and macOS) cannot run a script saved with CRLF. Git for Windows' own sh happens to tolerate it.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# The phone-bundle conformance fixture is compared byte for byte by a test in every checkout (Windows CI included):
# its notes stay LF whatever core.autocrlf says, and the bundle itself is binary (never line-converted).
tests/Dictum.Tests/Fixtures/Bundles/*.md text eol=lf
*.dictum binary
